  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "FPD-Drive and SimVTA both address the challenge of learning future behaviors in autonomous driving, with FPD-Drive focusing on distilling future knowledge through multi-target supervision and SimVTA leveraging simulation-grounded video supervision to improve planning and safety.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "FPD-Drive introduces Future-Privileged Multi-Target Distillation to transfer diverse, high-quality trajectory targets.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SimVTA prioritizes high-error futures among high-reward trajectories for better safety and planning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both methods improve PDMS and EPDMS scores by incorporating visual supervision beyond real-world driving logs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
